# Keep the build context lean and enforce DEP-001 at the context level too: the worker tier,
# the venv, caches, tests, docs, and snapshots never enter the image even if a COPY got sloppy.
.git/
.github/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# DEP-001: the GPU/worker world is never deployed (D-004/D-018).
worker/

# Not runtime: tests, docs, scratch scripts, snapshots, and the dev lock.
tests/
docs/
scripts/
*.zip
requirements-dev.txt
requirements-dev.lock

# ⚠⚠ ONE EXCEPTION, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY ONE FILE AND NOT THE DIRECTORY.
# The census feature ingest has to run somewhere with both a DATABASE_URL and the artifact. On
# the machine is the better place: the credential never leaves it, which is how migration 0010
# was applied. But `COPY scripts/` would put all 60 scripts on the production host, SEVEN of
# which write — including `fit_scorer.py`, which creates ranking runs and refits.
# ⚠ `D-079` decision 1 forbids a refit outright ("no refit — ranking_run id=2 is read from its
# row"). Shipping the fitter to production would put a forbidden operation one `fly ssh` away
# and behind no guard at all. A convenience is not worth converting a ruled prohibition into an
# honour system.
!scripts/census_ingest_features.py

# DEMO-ONLY: the miniature-demo notebook and its GPU dependency world never enter the
# image (ORDERS 2026-07-30 §1). The Dockerfile already COPYs only app/core/db/data + the
# runtime lock, so this is belt-and-braces against a future sloppy COPY dragging the
# notebook's torch/transformers world into the serving tier (DEP-001).
notebooks/
requirements-notebook.txt

# DEP-006: ui/ source is needed by build stage 1, but never its node_modules or dist —
# stage 1 runs npm ci + npm run build itself; shipping them would balloon the build context.
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
